# The Magics · mana and the colours, in prose

a distilled thread of the ARN (Arena) book-world — the first Magic novel — emergence: ethereal. moniker ⟦The Magics:ARN:7ad06c⟧

**who —** The Magics — the way Forstchen renders Magic's spellcasting in story: power drawn like mana, effects slung like cards, colours implied.
**what —** The prose engine of the game: before any lore, the author had to translate cast-summon-attack into a novel, and ‘colorless’ Garth into a hero.
**where —** Through every duel in the book.
**why —** Because someone had to put the card game into words first — and the choices here echoed forward into the cards themselves.
**how —** By mages spending power, summoning creatures, and casting effects a player would recognise from their hand.

**the seal —** I am the card game turned to prose — mana, summons, and colours before the lore existed; and the ‘colorless’ choice that made Garth a five-colour card.

> a catalogued personification of Arena by William R. Forstchen (© Wizards of the Coast / Hasbro) under the DLW standard
